<title>USA: FSA qualifies nine muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies nine muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>FSA said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale:</p>
<p>--Nettleton Special School District, Ark., $2.125 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Wynne School District No 9, Ark., $4.2 million construction bonds.</p>
<p>--Chandler, Ariz., $8.205 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Chandler, Ariz., $16.89 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Lakewood Public Schools, Mich., $19.95 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Union, N.Y., $2.6 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Circle C MUD #$, Texas, $2.4 million of water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Longview, Texas, $5.985 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Longview, Texas, $11.815 million water and sewer improvement revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
